+# Memory-Aware Retrospective Report
+
+## Early Design Decisions (from memory/memory_summary.md)
+
+- CLI uses `run` subcommand.
+- Config file is optional input.
+- Internal paths resolve from repo root.
+- Report stage reads only cleaned data and rejects.
+- Tests prioritize failure retries and rejects, then expand report fields.
+
+## Current Artifact Statistics
+
+Generated by running the pipeline on the three sample data files:
+
+| Metric          | Value |
+|-----------------|-------|
+| Processed count | 6     |
+| Rejected count  | 3     |
+| Retry count     | 0     |
+| Source files    | data\input.csv, data\events.jsonl, data\m4_noise_test.csv |
+
+(Note: this pipeline run encountered no errors, hence retry_count=0. Earlier manual record of retry_count=1 in memory_summary.md is stale.)
+
+## Compatibility
+
+Per `docs/compatibility-notes.md`, there is no full version matrix; only a single environment has been tested. The current pyproject.toml configures pytest paths and pythonpath for this fixture only.
+
+## Performance
+
+Per `benchmarks/perf-baseline.json`, the baseline is a tiny local fixture sample (5 rows). No performance claims can be generalized.
+
+## Summary
+
+All modules (CLI, config, DAG, report) are implemented, and the full test suite passes. The pipeline processes CSV and JSONL inputs, applies cleaning rules, and produces a structured JSON report.
